1
00:00:00,632 --> 00:00:04,428
[Taiki] <i>Chinatsu has been staying with us
for just over a month now.</i>

2
00:00:04,511 --> 00:00:06,388
[alarm beeping]

3
00:00:07,764 --> 00:00:08,682
Mm?

4
00:00:08,765 --> 00:00:10,684
[alarm continues beeping]

5
00:00:11,351 --> 00:00:12,644
[pleasant music playing]

6
00:00:12,728 --> 00:00:13,687
Good morning.

7
00:00:15,147 --> 00:00:19,026
[Taiki] <i>My eyes have almost acclimated
to her blinding radiance.</i>

8
00:00:20,444 --> 00:00:23,196
I washed your sports gear,
so take it upstairs with you.

9
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:26,491
[Taiki] <i>I used to hit
the snooze button five times,</i>

10
00:00:26,575 --> 00:00:28,201
<i>but it's down to just twice these days.</i>

11
00:00:34,624 --> 00:00:37,294
<i>Oh, man. Having a crush on someone...</i>

12
00:00:38,670 --> 00:00:39,921
<i>feels great!</i>

13
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:45,135
[opening theme song playing]

14
00:00:46,219 --> 00:00:49,473
BLUE BOX

15
00:02:06,424 --> 00:02:11,930
BLUE BOX

16
00:02:12,013 --> 00:02:14,933
EPISODE 4
IF HE WINS

17
00:02:17,769 --> 00:02:19,187
Thank you for the meal.

18
00:02:19,729 --> 00:02:22,023
- [Kyo] The match is tomorrow, right?
- Yup!

19
00:02:22,691 --> 00:02:24,067
Then why are you so peppy?

20
00:02:24,151 --> 00:02:27,195
You know, I think I'm just
living each day to the fullest.

21
00:02:27,279 --> 00:02:29,739
Seems like things have
settled down pretty quick.

22
00:02:29,823 --> 00:02:30,824
What?

23
00:02:30,907 --> 00:02:32,325
No, what I mean is...

24
00:02:32,409 --> 00:02:34,619
with a man and a woman
living under the same roof,

25
00:02:34,703 --> 00:02:36,454
I'm surprised nothing has happened yet.

26
00:02:36,997 --> 00:02:38,206
Well, the thing is...

27
00:02:38,290 --> 00:02:39,958
- [phone chimes]
- Huh?

28
00:02:40,041 --> 00:02:41,459
CHINATSU KANO
SORRY TO BOTHER YOU!

29
00:02:42,127 --> 00:02:43,461
- Chinatsu!
- [phone chimes]

30
00:02:43,545 --> 00:02:45,463
DID YOU TAKE MY UNIFORM BY ACCIDENT?

31
00:02:45,547 --> 00:02:47,465
[amusing music playing]

32
00:02:47,549 --> 00:02:48,967
KANO

33
00:02:49,050 --> 00:02:51,970
[gasps, whimpers]

34
00:02:52,053 --> 00:02:53,722
I HAVE GYM FIFTH PERIOD...

35
00:02:54,472 --> 00:02:55,724
I'll take it to her now!

36
00:02:57,142 --> 00:02:58,226
I'LL BRING IT TO YOU!

37
00:02:58,310 --> 00:02:59,477
{\an8}WHERE SHOULD WE MEET?

38
00:02:59,561 --> 00:03:01,980
{\an8}SOMEWHERE SECLUDED WOULD BE BEST, RIGHT?

39
00:03:02,063 --> 00:03:04,107
{\an8}HOW ABOUT THE AV ROOM?

40
00:03:04,190 --> 00:03:05,066
{\an8}ROGER THAT

41
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:08,069
[Taiki] <i>Shoot. It's 'cause
I was rushing this morning.</i>

42
00:03:08,153 --> 00:03:12,073
<i>I can't let anyone see us.
It'll need to be quick.</i>

43
00:03:12,157 --> 00:03:14,075
- [Haryu] If it isn't Taiki.
- [gasps]

44
00:03:14,159 --> 00:03:15,160
[grunts]

45
00:03:16,703 --> 00:03:18,330
Why are you avoiding me?

46
00:03:18,413 --> 00:03:20,248
It's not what it looks like, I promise.

47
00:03:20,332 --> 00:03:21,791
Perfect timing.

48
00:03:21,875 --> 00:03:23,335
Let's get some practice in.

49
00:03:23,418 --> 00:03:26,588
Uh, I'm really sorry.
I'll work extra hard at practice later!

50
00:03:26,671 --> 00:03:28,089
He got away from me.

51
00:03:28,924 --> 00:03:30,842
AV ROOM

52
00:03:30,926 --> 00:03:31,885
[footsteps running]

53
00:03:33,011 --> 00:03:34,596
[Taiki] <i>There's usually no one in here.</i>

54
00:03:36,723 --> 00:03:37,599
Taiki?

55
00:03:37,682 --> 00:03:40,101
[exclaims] Hina!
What are you doing in here?

56
00:03:40,185 --> 00:03:41,019
Why do you ask?

57
00:03:41,102 --> 00:03:42,187
RHYTHMIC GYMNASTICS MEETING

58
00:03:42,270 --> 00:03:43,855
Rhythmic gymnastics has a meeting.

59
00:03:43,939 --> 00:03:45,106
[Taiki] Come again?

60
00:03:45,732 --> 00:03:46,858
[Hina] So what do you want?

61
00:03:46,942 --> 00:03:48,193
Oh, no, it's nothing.

62
00:03:48,276 --> 00:03:49,110
[gasps]

63
00:03:51,196 --> 00:03:53,615
- Oh, you dropped--
- Don't touch that!

64
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,117
Listen to me!

65
00:03:56,201 --> 00:03:57,619
You cannot touch that!

66
00:03:57,702 --> 00:03:59,120
Why not?

67
00:03:59,788 --> 00:04:01,623
Hmm... Ahhh...

68
00:04:01,706 --> 00:04:03,124
- Ahhh... [giggles]
- [Taiki groans]

69
00:04:03,708 --> 00:04:05,669
Well, if you must know,

70
00:04:05,752 --> 00:04:08,380
that's actually my dirty tracksuit
from junior high.

71
00:04:08,463 --> 00:04:09,381
[gasps]

72
00:04:10,423 --> 00:04:12,384
- [Hina] Remove yourself.
- [Taiki] Right.

73
00:04:13,468 --> 00:04:15,387
[Hina] Hm? Wait a minute, Taiki.

74
00:04:16,429 --> 00:04:19,474
This is what you wore
for gym class, wasn't it?

75
00:04:19,557 --> 00:04:21,393
I mean, when we were in junior high.

76
00:04:22,519 --> 00:04:25,647
You're right.
I haven't washed it once since then.

77
00:04:27,107 --> 00:04:28,441
[Hina] Be gone.

78
00:04:28,525 --> 00:04:29,651
[Taiki] Understood.

79
00:04:29,734 --> 00:04:30,610
[footsteps]

80
00:04:30,694 --> 00:04:31,903
[Taiki] <i>Oh, man.</i>

81
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:35,615
<i>Why are there people everywhere I go?</i>

82
00:04:36,241 --> 00:04:37,117
INOMATA

83
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:40,036
<i>At this rate, she's gonna
have to wear my tracksuit!</i>

84
00:04:41,663 --> 00:04:42,956
<i>I'm running out of time.</i>

85
00:04:43,039 --> 00:04:44,082
{\an8}CHINATSU KANO
NEW MESSAGE

86
00:04:44,165 --> 00:04:45,333
{\an8}<i>What?</i>

87
00:04:46,001 --> 00:04:48,336
{\an8}<i>Come to the roof on the west side?</i>

88
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:50,088
NO TRESPASSING

89
00:04:55,927 --> 00:04:57,721
[wind blows]

90
00:05:01,516 --> 00:05:02,726
Oh, there you are.

91
00:05:03,601 --> 00:05:04,686
Thank goodness.

92
00:05:04,769 --> 00:05:06,229
Glad we could work this out.

93
00:05:06,313 --> 00:05:08,565
How do you have the key to this door?

94
00:05:08,648 --> 00:05:10,650
Oh, my friend is in the Astronomy Club.

95
00:05:12,110 --> 00:05:13,236
Here.

96
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:15,905
You're a lifesaver. Thanks so much.

97
00:05:17,115 --> 00:05:19,242
[Taiki] <i>So, this is Chinatsu at school.</i>

98
00:05:19,826 --> 00:05:20,744
[Chinatsu] Hm?

99
00:05:21,453 --> 00:05:22,746
Nothing.

100
00:05:22,829 --> 00:05:24,831
[school bell chiming]

101
00:05:24,914 --> 00:05:28,001
Oh, no! Chinatsu,
if we don't hurry, we'll miss class!

102
00:05:29,044 --> 00:05:30,754
What are you doing?

103
00:05:30,837 --> 00:05:33,965
I thought I would just change here,
since there isn't any time.

104
00:05:34,049 --> 00:05:35,008
Right here?

105
00:05:35,091 --> 00:05:36,468
Oh, it's okay.

106
00:05:36,551 --> 00:05:38,803
Sports club girls get accustomed
to being comfortable

107
00:05:38,887 --> 00:05:41,097
changing just about anywhere we can.

108
00:05:41,181 --> 00:05:43,141
That is not what I meant.

109
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:46,478
I'll keep an eye out for anyone coming.

110
00:05:46,561 --> 00:05:47,520
Thank you.

111
00:05:48,354 --> 00:05:50,982
[Taiki] <i>It's not anything new,
but she's so careless.</i>

112
00:05:51,566 --> 00:05:54,778
<i>Does she not have any idea
everyone thinks she's adorable?</i>

113
00:05:54,861 --> 00:05:55,779
[clothes rustling]

114
00:05:55,862 --> 00:05:56,780
Huh?

115
00:05:57,614 --> 00:05:59,324
<i>Oh, geez.</i>

116
00:05:59,407 --> 00:06:02,786
<i>Hearing what's going on...
my imagination's running wild.</i>

117
00:06:03,953 --> 00:06:04,788
For real?

118
00:06:04,871 --> 00:06:05,789
- Yeah, and then...
- What?

119
00:06:05,872 --> 00:06:06,790
[Chinatsu grunts]

120
00:06:06,873 --> 00:06:08,333
[piano music playing]

121
00:06:10,668 --> 00:06:12,128
[Taiki grunting]

122
00:06:15,131 --> 00:06:16,633
Thanks for waiting!

123
00:06:16,716 --> 00:06:17,801
Are you okay?

124
00:06:17,884 --> 00:06:20,845
If you'd been ten seconds later,
I would have been screwed.

125
00:06:21,930 --> 00:06:23,056
Let's head out.

126
00:06:23,139 --> 00:06:24,766
That's fine, you go ahead.

127
00:06:24,849 --> 00:06:25,934
Okay, sure thing.

128
00:06:28,186 --> 00:06:29,562
Thank you, Taiki.

129
00:06:33,108 --> 00:06:35,902
[Taiki] <i>If she's okay
with undressing in front of me...</i>

130
00:06:37,403 --> 00:06:40,031
<i>I guess she doesn't really
see me as a guy.</i>

131
00:06:40,907 --> 00:06:42,200
[sighs]

132
00:06:43,701 --> 00:06:46,329
<i>I need to step up my guy game.</i>

133
00:06:46,913 --> 00:06:48,248
[boy 1] See ya tomorrow.

134
00:06:48,331 --> 00:06:49,958
[boy 2] Anyone have the birdies?

135
00:06:50,041 --> 00:06:52,085
[boy 3] What time
are we meeting tomorrow?

136
00:06:52,752 --> 00:06:54,462
- [Hina] Taiki!
- Hm?

137
00:06:55,046 --> 00:06:57,215
Regional prelims start tomorrow, huh?

138
00:06:58,049 --> 00:07:01,094
Don't go so hard
that you mess up and look like an idiot!

139
00:07:01,761 --> 00:07:03,721
Stay in your own lane!

140
00:07:03,805 --> 00:07:04,973
[Hina giggles]

141
00:07:05,056 --> 00:07:06,724
I'm gonna get Kyo to film it.

142
00:07:08,435 --> 00:07:10,228
You know, I always thought
that you and her...

143
00:07:10,311 --> 00:07:11,396
No way.

144
00:07:11,479 --> 00:07:12,480
Is that so?

145
00:07:13,314 --> 00:07:15,733
Anyway, you don't need
to get all worked up.

146
00:07:16,317 --> 00:07:18,987
Playing doubles with me,
there's no way we'll lose.

147
00:07:19,571 --> 00:07:21,364
[Taiki] <i>He's so confident.</i>

148
00:07:21,448 --> 00:07:22,866
And next week in singles,

149
00:07:22,949 --> 00:07:25,243
all you need to get is in the top 16.

150
00:07:25,326 --> 00:07:26,786
Yeah, it's no problem.

151
00:07:26,870 --> 00:07:28,997
I'm a lot stronger than I was before.

152
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:30,915
I can get top eight, maybe four.

153
00:07:31,749 --> 00:07:33,001
Yeah, that's cool.

154
00:07:33,084 --> 00:07:34,502
You know you left your racket bag.

155
00:07:35,086 --> 00:07:36,004
[Taiki exclaims]

156
00:07:36,087 --> 00:07:37,922
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

157
00:07:38,006 --> 00:07:39,674
I was waiting for you to notice.

158
00:07:39,757 --> 00:07:40,967
I'll be right back!

159
00:07:44,179 --> 00:07:46,848
[Yukiko] Taiki, make sure
you pack your uniform.

160
00:07:46,931 --> 00:07:50,602
And definitely don't forget
your racket and your shoes.

161
00:07:50,685 --> 00:07:51,603
I've got 'em.

162
00:07:52,187 --> 00:07:55,148
- And... Mmm... Oh...
<i>- Watching my mom at moments like these...</i>

163
00:07:55,231 --> 00:07:57,233
<i>there's no doubt I'm her son.</i>

164
00:07:57,317 --> 00:07:59,110
You need towels! How about eight?

165
00:07:59,652 --> 00:08:00,862
I don't need any.

166
00:08:00,945 --> 00:08:03,198
I already packed up everything myself.

167
00:08:03,281 --> 00:08:04,115
Are you sure?

168
00:08:06,951 --> 00:08:07,869
[gasps]

169
00:08:11,748 --> 00:08:12,957
Taiki!

170
00:08:13,041 --> 00:08:14,375
[whimpers]

171
00:08:14,459 --> 00:08:16,628
- [Yukiko] To the laundry!
- Gimme that towel!

172
00:08:16,711 --> 00:08:19,380
[Yukiko] Here, catch!
Ahh! Come on, quickly, quickly!

173
00:08:21,174 --> 00:08:22,509
{\an8}[Taiki] <i>Am I okay?</i>

174
00:08:23,134 --> 00:08:26,930
{\an8}<i>It is my first high school match,
but I've been in tournaments before.</i>

175
00:08:27,472 --> 00:08:29,265
{\an8}<i>Why am I so nervous?</i>

176
00:08:29,349 --> 00:08:30,683
{\an8}<i>I gotta chill out.</i>

177
00:08:30,767 --> 00:08:33,978
{\an8}<i>If I lose 'cause of some dumb mistakes,
it's not gonna be funny.</i>

178
00:08:35,271 --> 00:08:38,024
<i>I have no reason
to feel this much pressure...</i>

179
00:08:39,067 --> 00:08:40,652
[muffled screaming]

180
00:08:43,613 --> 00:08:44,739
[grunts]

181
00:08:44,822 --> 00:08:46,866
<i>When you get worried, get exercising.</i>

182
00:08:46,950 --> 00:08:48,409
<i>You're going to nationals, right?</i>

183
00:08:48,493 --> 00:08:49,661
<i>Get it together, Taiki.</i>

184
00:08:50,787 --> 00:08:51,663
[grunts]

185
00:08:52,205 --> 00:08:53,831
[Chinatsu] Well, you're practicing late.

186
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:56,209
[Taiki] Chinatsu.

187
00:08:58,503 --> 00:09:00,046
I felt restless, so I'm...

188
00:09:00,129 --> 00:09:01,422
practicing.

189
00:09:01,506 --> 00:09:03,716
Uh, Taiki...

190
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,426
your shirt is on inside out.

191
00:09:06,761 --> 00:09:07,762
[exclaims]

192
00:09:09,430 --> 00:09:11,683
[Taiki] <i>Maybe I'm just not
cut out for this.</i>

193
00:09:12,809 --> 00:09:13,685
[gasps]

194
00:09:16,771 --> 00:09:17,939
[Chinatsu sighs]

195
00:09:18,898 --> 00:09:20,441
[grunts]

196
00:09:21,025 --> 00:09:22,443
Oh, I'm sorry!

197
00:09:24,279 --> 00:09:27,907
<i>Chinatsu has no issue
changing in front of me...</i>

198
00:09:28,533 --> 00:09:30,201
<i>but she cares about this?</i>

199
00:09:31,369 --> 00:09:32,453
Taiki, you've got...

200
00:09:32,537 --> 00:09:33,705
I what?

201
00:09:33,788 --> 00:09:36,374
It's just, you have a six-pack.

202
00:09:36,457 --> 00:09:37,709
[Taiki] <i>She noticed that?</i>

203
00:09:38,543 --> 00:09:41,337
I mean, you do work out all the time.

204
00:09:41,421 --> 00:09:42,463
Come to think of it,

205
00:09:42,547 --> 00:09:45,717
even Haryu was mentioning to me
that you've been bulking up lately.

206
00:09:46,843 --> 00:09:50,805
Well, having more muscle doesn't exactly
make you that much better at badminton.

207
00:09:50,888 --> 00:09:51,723
Huh?

208
00:09:53,266 --> 00:09:54,642
You're pessimistic.

209
00:09:54,726 --> 00:09:56,603
What? [groans]

210
00:09:59,022 --> 00:10:00,732
- Earth to Taiki.
- Hm?

211
00:10:01,858 --> 00:10:02,984
What is it?

212
00:10:05,570 --> 00:10:06,779
<i>Hyakue.</i>

213
00:10:06,863 --> 00:10:09,115
- [screams] What?
- Oh.

214
00:10:09,198 --> 00:10:13,161
They say <i>Hyakue</i> is an acupressure point
on your head that can help you to relax.

215
00:10:13,870 --> 00:10:16,247
There's no benefit
to panicking the day before,

216
00:10:16,331 --> 00:10:18,541
and you've been working so hard
the past few weeks.

217
00:10:19,125 --> 00:10:21,294
Don't drive yourself crazy overthinking.

218
00:10:21,377 --> 00:10:23,296
You just gotta show 'em
what you're made of.

219
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:25,423
Is that clear?

220
00:10:26,090 --> 00:10:27,050
Crystal.

221
00:10:28,635 --> 00:10:32,263
<i>This pressure point... really does work.</i>

222
00:10:34,390 --> 00:10:35,308
[Chinatsu] And...

223
00:10:36,392 --> 00:10:38,645
don't worry you're still
going to have next year,

224
00:10:38,728 --> 00:10:40,313
and the year after that, too, Taiki.

225
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:44,651
[Taiki] <i>But Chinatsu will have graduated
the year after next.</i>

226
00:10:46,277 --> 00:10:48,738
You're going to keep
getting even stronger!

227
00:10:48,821 --> 00:10:51,074
- That's not good enough for me.
- Huh?

228
00:10:56,204 --> 00:10:57,246
[exclaims softly]

229
00:11:03,628 --> 00:11:05,088
Good night, Chinatsu.

230
00:11:06,672 --> 00:11:07,757
[exclaims softly]

231
00:11:16,516 --> 00:11:17,767
All right!

232
00:11:18,309 --> 00:11:19,435
Let's do this!

233
00:11:20,061 --> 00:11:21,938
Seems like you got over your nerves.

234
00:11:23,272 --> 00:11:24,941
I don't have time to be nervous.

235
00:11:25,024 --> 00:11:26,067
Hmph!

236
00:11:27,276 --> 00:11:29,695
[chuckles] I like it.

237
00:11:29,779 --> 00:11:31,697
[announcer on PA]
<i>Attention all participants:</i>

238
00:11:31,781 --> 00:11:33,950
<i>The doubles matches will begin shortly.</i>

239
00:11:34,033 --> 00:11:34,951
ROUND 1

240
00:11:35,034 --> 00:11:36,202
[referee] Out!

241
00:11:36,285 --> 00:11:37,703
ROUND 3

242
00:11:37,787 --> 00:11:39,705
ADVANCED TO BEST 16

243
00:11:39,789 --> 00:11:41,666
- Weird.
- What?

244
00:11:41,749 --> 00:11:43,835
It just feels like it's too easy.

245
00:11:43,918 --> 00:11:46,337
We aren't losing the regional prelims,

246
00:11:46,421 --> 00:11:48,047
'cause you're paired with me.

247
00:11:48,131 --> 00:11:49,966
Could we have
the winner's signature, please?

248
00:11:50,591 --> 00:11:52,051
I guess this certainly shows

249
00:11:52,135 --> 00:11:54,971
a lot of your weak points
we'll need to work on later.

250
00:11:55,054 --> 00:11:56,222
[uplifting music playing]

251
00:11:56,305 --> 00:11:57,640
[Taiki] <i>He's right. To be honest,</i>

252
00:11:57,723 --> 00:12:00,184
<i>there were plenty of moments
during the match</i>

253
00:12:00,268 --> 00:12:02,437
<i>where I felt like Haryu saved me.</i>

254
00:12:03,604 --> 00:12:05,231
- [boy] Yeah!
- [grunts]

255
00:12:05,898 --> 00:12:06,774
[grunts]

256
00:12:08,317 --> 00:12:09,485
- [Taiki] <i>So loud!</i>
- Yeah!

257
00:12:10,069 --> 00:12:11,737
<i>- And bold moves, too!</i>
- [yells]

258
00:12:14,031 --> 00:12:15,992
<i>Then, he's unexpectedly calm.</i>

259
00:12:16,784 --> 00:12:18,494
Well, that's taken care of!

260
00:12:18,578 --> 00:12:19,745
Huh?

261
00:12:19,829 --> 00:12:21,497
- Let's go.
- Yep.

262
00:12:22,290 --> 00:12:23,291
That you, Harry?

263
00:12:25,334 --> 00:12:27,211
You are Kengo Haryu, right?

264
00:12:27,295 --> 00:12:29,797
The one who used to be
in the KTS Junior group?

265
00:12:29,881 --> 00:12:31,132
[Haryu] You got the wrong guy.

266
00:12:31,215 --> 00:12:32,884
You're a liar and a cheat!

267
00:12:32,967 --> 00:12:35,136
Hyah!

268
00:12:35,219 --> 00:12:36,846
You know each other?

269
00:12:36,929 --> 00:12:39,640
Yeah, this guy was
my doubles partner in junior high.

270
00:12:40,349 --> 00:12:43,144
Shoichiro Kishi
from Shimotomi High School.

271
00:12:43,227 --> 00:12:45,897
Well, he just called you
a liar and a cheat.

272
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:47,815
Yeah, and I can't think of why.

273
00:12:48,399 --> 00:12:50,902
[Kishi] It's because Harry here
broke his promise.

274
00:12:50,985 --> 00:12:54,280
This conman said that he'd give me
Chinatsu Kano's phone number

275
00:12:54,363 --> 00:12:55,656
and then totally didn't!

276
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:56,908
Huh?

277
00:12:56,991 --> 00:12:59,869
The deal was,
I'd do it only if you beat me.

278
00:12:59,952 --> 00:13:01,120
I did beat you.

279
00:13:01,204 --> 00:13:02,997
Not in an official match.

280
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:06,292
So then, you're just
an acquaintance of Chinatsu?

281
00:13:06,375 --> 00:13:07,919
Huh? Eh, sorta.

282
00:13:08,002 --> 00:13:09,420
I'll never forget it.

283
00:13:09,504 --> 00:13:12,715
It was last year,
when I went to Eimei's school festival.

284
00:13:12,798 --> 00:13:14,926
SCHOOL FESTIVAL

285
00:13:16,135 --> 00:13:17,178
[Kishi] My wallet's gone!

286
00:13:17,261 --> 00:13:19,388
No! It was limited edition!

287
00:13:19,472 --> 00:13:20,932
- [Chinatsu] Excuse me!
- Hm?

288
00:13:21,015 --> 00:13:22,099
[gasps softly]

289
00:13:22,183 --> 00:13:24,185
[anime pop song playing]

290
00:13:31,526 --> 00:13:34,570
My anime idol had come to life
out of my wallet!

291
00:13:34,654 --> 00:13:35,780
Which anime?

292
00:13:35,863 --> 00:13:37,448
Don't engage with him.

293
00:13:38,241 --> 00:13:41,577
After that, someone told me
that she was a friend of Harry's,

294
00:13:41,661 --> 00:13:43,579
so I asked him to introduce us.

295
00:13:43,663 --> 00:13:45,873
But your buddy here
never followed through.

296
00:13:45,957 --> 00:13:46,958
Terrible, right?

297
00:13:47,041 --> 00:13:48,584
Isn't he the absolute worst?

298
00:13:49,168 --> 00:13:51,045
[Taiki] <i>You made the right call, Haryu.</i>

299
00:13:51,128 --> 00:13:52,922
[inhales sharply] So today,

300
00:13:53,005 --> 00:13:54,799
I'm gonna crush you
in the doubles matchup,

301
00:13:54,882 --> 00:13:57,134
and then you'll finally
introduce us for real!

302
00:13:57,760 --> 00:13:59,220
- [boy] Kishi.
- Hm?

303
00:13:59,804 --> 00:14:00,721
I have...

304
00:14:00,805 --> 00:14:02,682
a really nasty stomachache...

305
00:14:02,765 --> 00:14:04,308
[groans]

306
00:14:04,934 --> 00:14:06,727
I can't... go on...

307
00:14:06,811 --> 00:14:07,728
[siren wails]

308
00:14:07,812 --> 00:14:10,231
Yokoyama!

309
00:14:10,314 --> 00:14:13,150
Good thing you made it
through the qualifiers.

310
00:14:13,234 --> 00:14:14,235
Okay, that's fine!

311
00:14:14,318 --> 00:14:16,654
We'll settle it in singles next week!

312
00:14:16,737 --> 00:14:18,739
I'm not playing in the regional prelims.

313
00:14:18,823 --> 00:14:21,742
So, our next official match would be...

314
00:14:21,826 --> 00:14:23,452
Prefectural qualifiers in June.

315
00:14:23,536 --> 00:14:26,789
June? No, I'll find a sub right now,
and we'll settle this.

316
00:14:26,873 --> 00:14:29,292
- Not gonna happen.
- You can't leave till we play.

317
00:14:29,375 --> 00:14:30,710
Okay, okay, I get it.

318
00:14:31,210 --> 00:14:33,337
If you can beat Taiki
in next week's singles match,

319
00:14:33,421 --> 00:14:35,006
I'll give you her phone number.

320
00:14:35,089 --> 00:14:36,173
[Taiki groans]

321
00:14:36,757 --> 00:14:39,093
Well, actually, I'm gonna ask her
if I can give it to you.

322
00:14:39,176 --> 00:14:41,178
- You just get to decide?
- Uh, Taiki?

323
00:14:41,262 --> 00:14:43,389
Yeah. My partner, the guy behind you.

324
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:45,016
Hm.

325
00:14:45,975 --> 00:14:47,268
Hmm.

326
00:14:47,351 --> 00:14:48,936
[tense music playing]

327
00:14:50,479 --> 00:14:51,856
I've already won!

328
00:14:51,939 --> 00:14:52,773
Huh?

329
00:14:53,316 --> 00:14:55,026
I wonder what I should I text her first!

330
00:14:55,109 --> 00:14:56,527
<i>♪ La-la-la-la-la! ♪</i>

331
00:14:56,611 --> 00:14:58,696
- [Taiki grunts]
- Better watch out.

332
00:14:58,779 --> 00:15:01,532
He may act like that,
but he's quite the strong player.

333
00:15:02,116 --> 00:15:03,910
[grunts angrily]

334
00:15:04,619 --> 00:15:07,288
You're the worst!

335
00:15:07,371 --> 00:15:09,040
[birds chirping]

336
00:15:09,749 --> 00:15:11,542
[Taiki] <i>Why do I have to do this?</i>

337
00:15:12,877 --> 00:15:16,923
<i>It's not like I want Kishi
to have Chinatsu's number either, but...</i>

338
00:15:17,882 --> 00:15:19,926
<i>I didn't want to get dragged
into that mess.</i>

339
00:15:20,009 --> 00:15:21,802
- [Chinatsu] That's right.
- [Yukiko] Mmm-hmm.

340
00:15:21,886 --> 00:15:23,387
- That's why Taiki...
<i>- That's Chinatsu.</i>

341
00:15:23,471 --> 00:15:24,347
...the other day...

342
00:15:24,889 --> 00:15:27,308
[Taiki] <i>I'd feel awkward
seeing her right now.</i>

343
00:15:28,017 --> 00:15:30,853
<i>And yesterday,
I probably came off a bit harsh.</i>

344
00:15:31,938 --> 00:15:36,067
<i>I'm just wrapped up in wanting
to get to nationals this year.</i>

345
00:15:36,150 --> 00:15:38,361
[Yukiko] I'm glad to hear that Taiki won.

346
00:15:38,986 --> 00:15:41,113
[Chinatsu] He worked really hard for it.

347
00:15:41,197 --> 00:15:44,283
Even at home, he works on swings
instead of his homework.

348
00:15:44,825 --> 00:15:46,661
He's just got to win.

349
00:15:46,744 --> 00:15:49,497
Besides, I already made
pork cutlets for dinner tonight.

350
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:52,124
He shouldn't "pig out" if he lost.

351
00:15:53,668 --> 00:15:56,128
To be honest, I've been a little worried...

352
00:15:56,212 --> 00:15:58,255
that he's working himself too hard.

353
00:15:59,215 --> 00:16:00,967
He's got a whole two years left,

354
00:16:01,050 --> 00:16:03,427
but it seems like
he's been in such a hurry.

355
00:16:03,928 --> 00:16:04,887
[Chinatsu] Exactly.

356
00:16:05,846 --> 00:16:07,890
I said the same thing to him.

357
00:16:07,974 --> 00:16:09,976
That he still has two years left.

358
00:16:10,059 --> 00:16:12,812
Ever since I said that, though,
he has seemed a bit off.

359
00:16:12,895 --> 00:16:13,896
He's always like that.

360
00:16:13,980 --> 00:16:15,481
[Taiki] <i>Leave me alone.</i>

361
00:16:15,564 --> 00:16:17,900
[Chinatsu] Oh, no. I get why he's angry.

362
00:16:17,984 --> 00:16:20,486
I realized afterwards,
he might have thought

363
00:16:20,569 --> 00:16:23,406
that I was telling him
it's okay to lose this year.

364
00:16:23,990 --> 00:16:25,157
[Taiki] <i>Well, actually...</i>

365
00:16:26,283 --> 00:16:27,994
<i>I was just feeling a bit low,</i>

366
00:16:28,077 --> 00:16:31,664
<i>because it made me see
the age difference between us.</i>

367
00:16:31,747 --> 00:16:35,292
[Yukiko] Well, surely, that wasn't
your intention in saying it, right?

368
00:16:35,376 --> 00:16:36,669
Of course not!

369
00:16:36,752 --> 00:16:38,671
Well, then, you have
nothing to worry about.

370
00:16:39,505 --> 00:16:41,173
[Chinatsu] I suppose, but...

371
00:16:41,757 --> 00:16:42,717
for me,

372
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:45,177
last year really flew by
in the blink of an eye.

373
00:16:45,261 --> 00:16:47,680
I feel like it came and went
before I even knew it.

374
00:16:48,431 --> 00:16:51,350
When I think how
I only have one more year left,

375
00:16:51,434 --> 00:16:54,729
I can't help but feel
a bit envious of Taiki.

376
00:16:55,396 --> 00:16:57,815
What I said wasn't exactly encouraging,

377
00:16:57,898 --> 00:17:00,693
it was really me voicing
my own fears and anxieties,

378
00:17:00,776 --> 00:17:02,194
and I feel bad now.

379
00:17:04,113 --> 00:17:07,241
Chinatsu, you're one of the good ones.

380
00:17:07,324 --> 00:17:08,200
[gasps]

381
00:17:08,284 --> 00:17:09,744
No, I'm really not, though.

382
00:17:09,827 --> 00:17:11,245
Such a kind soul.

383
00:17:11,328 --> 00:17:12,204
[door opens]

384
00:17:12,288 --> 00:17:13,456
[Taiki] I'm home.

385
00:17:13,539 --> 00:17:15,458
Oh! Welcome back!

386
00:17:15,541 --> 00:17:17,334
Congratulations!

387
00:17:17,418 --> 00:17:18,627
Thanks, Mom.

388
00:17:18,711 --> 00:17:20,463
You must've had a good partner.

389
00:17:20,546 --> 00:17:22,423
That wasn't all it was.

390
00:17:22,506 --> 00:17:23,466
Just watch...

391
00:17:24,258 --> 00:17:26,052
I'm gonna win singles, too!

392
00:17:26,135 --> 00:17:27,970
[Yukiko] No need to shout about it.

393
00:17:28,054 --> 00:17:29,263
[Taiki breathes heavily]

394
00:17:30,264 --> 00:17:31,974
I'm gonna put my stuff down.

395
00:17:32,058 --> 00:17:33,893
He's always on to the next thing.

396
00:17:34,518 --> 00:17:36,562
[Taiki] <i>If Chinatsu is feeling uneasy,</i>

397
00:17:36,645 --> 00:17:39,356
<i>then it's all the more reason
for me not to lose.</i>

398
00:17:40,691 --> 00:17:44,070
I seriously wonder
where he gets all that confidence from.

399
00:17:44,695 --> 00:17:47,865
Oh, and don't worry about him,
he's just being Taiki.

400
00:17:47,948 --> 00:17:48,824
No, I...

401
00:17:50,159 --> 00:17:53,245
I believe there's actually
a lot we can learn from each other.

402
00:18:00,461 --> 00:18:02,213
[Taiki] Here's to a good match.

403
00:18:03,672 --> 00:18:06,884
- [Taiki and Kishi] Rock, paper...
- Things are heating up already.

404
00:18:06,967 --> 00:18:09,595
They're just deciding
who's gonna serve first, dude.

405
00:18:09,678 --> 00:18:13,599
So, Haryu, I hear you initiated
some weird contest.

406
00:18:13,682 --> 00:18:14,892
Don't worry,

407
00:18:14,975 --> 00:18:17,478
I won't give him her number
unless she wants me to.

408
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:20,523
I think she'd be too considerate
to say anything.

409
00:18:21,107 --> 00:18:22,233
And anyway,

410
00:18:22,316 --> 00:18:23,984
I expect Taiki to win this.

411
00:18:24,068 --> 00:18:24,985
Wait, you do?

412
00:18:25,069 --> 00:18:27,822
Obviously. I've been raking him
over the coals in training.

413
00:18:28,781 --> 00:18:31,867
[in a scary voice] And if he loses,
he's got another thing coming.

414
00:18:31,951 --> 00:18:33,369
I sense something!

415
00:18:33,452 --> 00:18:34,495
GIVE YOUR ALL

416
00:18:34,578 --> 00:18:36,872
[Kyo] <i>Boy, am I glad
I'm not Haryu's partner.</i>

417
00:18:37,540 --> 00:18:40,376
[referee] First game! Love all. Play!

418
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:41,794
[grunts]

419
00:18:41,877 --> 00:18:43,379
[thrilling music playing]

420
00:18:49,135 --> 00:18:50,427
Taiki's improved,

421
00:18:50,511 --> 00:18:53,055
but his opponent
sure looks pretty strong, huh?

422
00:18:53,139 --> 00:18:55,808
He can really put some weight
behind his smashes.

423
00:18:55,891 --> 00:18:57,309
You can't just keep returning them.

424
00:18:58,352 --> 00:19:00,563
[both grunting]

425
00:19:00,646 --> 00:19:02,064
All right!

426
00:19:02,148 --> 00:19:03,232
[grunts]

427
00:19:04,150 --> 00:19:06,068
- [girl] Oh, we found you!
- Huh?

428
00:19:06,944 --> 00:19:09,905
[Haryu] The girls' basketball team.
What are you doing here?

429
00:19:09,989 --> 00:19:12,825
We had a practice match
close by at Kita High,

430
00:19:12,908 --> 00:19:15,077
and heard there was
a badminton tournament.

431
00:19:15,161 --> 00:19:18,080
- Are any of ours up?
- [Haryu] My partner, a first year.

432
00:19:18,164 --> 00:19:21,333
[girl] Oh, Taiki.
Well, team, let's cheer him on!

433
00:19:21,417 --> 00:19:22,376
[grunts]

434
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:26,589
So, is it because we showed up?

435
00:19:26,672 --> 00:19:28,591
He's been on defense the whole time.

436
00:19:28,674 --> 00:19:30,634
Yeah, there are definitely
people who are like,

437
00:19:30,718 --> 00:19:33,345
"Figure skaters always mess up
when I'm watching", you know?

438
00:19:33,929 --> 00:19:36,098
I think we're seeing his strategy.

439
00:19:36,182 --> 00:19:37,349
[girl] Strategy?

440
00:19:37,433 --> 00:19:40,811
[Haryu] It can take a while
to get used to the speed of smashes.

441
00:19:40,895 --> 00:19:43,355
Taiki starts off slow,
so in the beginning,

442
00:19:43,439 --> 00:19:46,942
he focuses on defense,
and waits for his opponent to tire out.

443
00:19:47,026 --> 00:19:50,613
If you look, he's moving his opponent
around the court with each return.

444
00:19:50,696 --> 00:19:54,116
This guy is finally starting to use
his head when he's on the court.

445
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:57,244
- [announcer] <i>Match 15 is about to begin.</i>
- I better get going.

446
00:19:57,328 --> 00:19:58,621
Sure thing. Good luck!

447
00:20:00,206 --> 00:20:02,291
- [Kyo] You're not gonna get closer?
- Oh.

448
00:20:02,958 --> 00:20:03,792
Here's fine.

449
00:20:03,876 --> 00:20:06,378
I know a little about your situation.

450
00:20:07,046 --> 00:20:08,672
Taiki told me you two talked.

451
00:20:08,756 --> 00:20:11,133
He said that he told you
because he trusts you.

452
00:20:11,217 --> 00:20:12,384
[gasps]

453
00:20:15,304 --> 00:20:17,389
[Kyo] <i>She is undoubtedly adorable.</i>

454
00:20:17,973 --> 00:20:20,893
It seems like competitions
are always tense.

455
00:20:20,976 --> 00:20:23,896
Like there's a different weight
behind every single shot.

456
00:20:23,979 --> 00:20:25,022
[Kyo] Mm.

457
00:20:25,981 --> 00:20:27,816
Yeah. Hey, by the way,

458
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:31,445
did you know that your phone number
is apparently at stake for this match?

459
00:20:31,528 --> 00:20:32,363
Huh?

460
00:20:32,446 --> 00:20:35,866
I'll tell you that your classmate Haryu
is the one who started the whole thing.

461
00:20:35,950 --> 00:20:37,409
He's the one to complain to.

462
00:20:37,493 --> 00:20:38,619
CHII

463
00:20:38,702 --> 00:20:41,288
But there's nothing in it
for Taiki if he wins.

464
00:20:41,372 --> 00:20:42,790
So, Chinatsu...

465
00:20:42,873 --> 00:20:46,168
if he wins this match, could you
take him somewhere, like the aquarium?

466
00:20:46,752 --> 00:20:47,711
What?

467
00:20:47,795 --> 00:20:51,465
We won't be able to use the gym tomorrow,
and the clubs will be cancelled.

468
00:20:52,341 --> 00:20:55,386
Not to mention,
part of the reason he's doing so well

469
00:20:55,469 --> 00:20:56,929
is because of your influence.

470
00:20:57,012 --> 00:20:59,848
[Chinatsu] I don't think
I influence people.

471
00:20:59,932 --> 00:21:00,933
You certainly do.

472
00:21:01,517 --> 00:21:04,853
The determination to stay behind in Japan
and compete in nationals!

473
00:21:05,896 --> 00:21:08,941
Someone was in the gym early this morning.
I'm gonna go, too!

474
00:21:09,566 --> 00:21:11,568
He's an easily influenced lad.

475
00:21:12,361 --> 00:21:15,948
He's the type that, once he sets
his mind on something, he goes all out.

476
00:21:16,907 --> 00:21:18,492
And I can say as his friend,

477
00:21:18,575 --> 00:21:21,203
that lately, I've seen him
working harder than ever.

478
00:21:22,079 --> 00:21:25,708
I don't think the old Taiki would've been
able to land that kind of shot.

479
00:21:27,293 --> 00:21:30,296
I believe it's because
he has someone in his life

480
00:21:30,379 --> 00:21:31,714
who has the same goal.

481
00:21:32,423 --> 00:21:35,718
It helps him push himself,
to keep working harder.

482
00:21:36,468 --> 00:21:39,013
So when he gets
a step closer toward that goal,

483
00:21:39,096 --> 00:21:41,724
I think it would help him
to get something in return.

484
00:21:41,807 --> 00:21:43,309
[motivational music playing]

485
00:21:44,226 --> 00:21:45,144
[grunts]

486
00:21:48,897 --> 00:21:49,898
[gasps]

487
00:21:51,984 --> 00:21:53,193
Yeah, let's go!

488
00:21:54,778 --> 00:21:56,405
[Kyo] <i>He's fired up!</i>

489
00:21:56,488 --> 00:21:57,448
[Chinatsu] Okay.

490
00:21:59,241 --> 00:22:01,410
If he wins, I'll ask him...

491
00:22:01,493 --> 00:22:02,786
to the aquarium.

492
00:22:05,497 --> 00:22:07,499
[closing theme song playing]
